    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm prepping for the upcoming trade summit in Jakarta. I really want to land a big impression and show the local delegates that I've actually done my homework on Indonesian nuances. I'm thinking of using the phrase \"Makan hati\" in my opening remarks to show I understand the struggles of the local industry. Is that's a safe, neutral idiom to use for rapport, or is it a bit risky?",
