      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your contact is correct; in certain high-level, informal settings, acknowledging deep struggle with \"makan hati\" can signal profound, authentic empathy. It suggests you understand the *real* cost of doing business, not just the spreadsheets. However, the risk remains that the tone can easily be misinterpreted as pity rather than solidarity, especially if your delivery isn't perfectly calibrated. If you use it, frame it immediately with a forward-looking commitment to *solving* that burden, turning the acknowledgment into a promise of partnership.",
