      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, and honestly, that's exactly the vibe I'm going for. I appreciate the nuanced take. \n\nOne more thing—I was looking at some social media posts from locals in Jakarta, and I saw a phrase that looked similar: \"makan garam\". It seems like they use it to describe someone with lots of experience, like \"having eaten a lot of salt.\" I'm thinking of pairing \"makan hati\" with \"makan garam\" to basically say, \"I've seen the struggle, and I have the experience to help.\" \n\nThat sounds like a killer, high-impact opening that shows I'm deeply connected to their culture, right? It's a very safe way to show I'm an experienced leader who cares, isn't it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
